Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||01-10-2000||04:41 PM||||btw I'm building a liquid cooled computer. Probably a celeron 400 (fairly cheap) but I'm not sure yet. I'm testing it on a 486 before I put it in an expensive system.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I get all sorts of reactions when I mention what I'm doing.. some people think it's the coolest thing they've ever heard.. others think I'm crazy, others laugh and say I should try a heatsink, so then I explain that just a heatsink isn't good enough when you're trying to run a CPU 200MHz over the rated speed...||||reg||1
